.TH TUXDOKU 6 "2026-11-11" "tuxdoku @VERSION@" "Games"
.SH NAME
tuxdoku \- cheerful penguin logic puzzle (Queens / Star Battle style)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxdoku
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen ]
.RB [ \-\-mute ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuxdoku
is a colourful logic puzzle. The N\(muN board is divided into N coloured
regions. Hide exactly one penguin in every row, every column and every
region so that no two penguins touch each other, not even diagonally.
Each level gives three lives; placing a penguin on a wrong cell costs one.
Lives left at the end of a level become hints for the next level
(at most N\-2 hints at a time). The board grows from 5\(mu5 to 10\(mu10.
The user interface is in Hungarian.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-mute
Do not open the audio device (no music, no sound effects).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left click
cycle a cell: empty, X mark, penguin, empty
.TP
.B Right click / drag
toggle X marks (dragging marks or clears many cells)
.TP
.B Arrow keys, Space/Enter, X, P, Backspace
move the cursor, cycle, X mark, penguin, clear
.TP
.B H
use a hint
.TP
.B M
music on/off
.TP
.BR S " or " N
sound effects on/off
.TP
.B F11
toggle fullscreen
.TP
.B Esc
back to the menu
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tuxdoku/progress.json
progress, settings and high scores (honours
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TUXDOKU_DATA_DIR
override the directory of
.IR progress.json .
